The env_0080 big-box retailer scenario (Northgate Stores, Inc.) is finished in `env/env_0080_big_box_general_merchandise_retailer/`, and every check I ran myself at the end passed. It took about 38 hours with roughly six account-limit cuts.

**Final state**

| Difficulty | Product | Policy audit | KB audit |
|---|---|---|---|
| membership_fees_and_benefits | membership (73 docs) | revision_7: both tasks PASS, charter CLEAN | revision_3: PASS, kb CLEAN |
| store_card_billing_and_disputes | card (53 docs) | revision_9: PASS, CLEAN | revision_2: PASS, CLEAN |
| protection_plan_claims_and_refunds | plan (62 docs) | revision_6: PASS, CLEAN | revision_3: PASS, CLEAN |
| order_returns_and_price_adjustments | order (56 docs) | revision_7: PASS, CLEAN | revision_4: PASS, CLEAN |
| marketplace_orders_and_guarantee | market (63 docs) | revision_12: PASS, CLEAN | revision_2: PASS, CLEAN |

The two unclaimed products, trade (20 docs) and gift (19 docs), are rendered with check_docs green. As the process prescribes for unclaimed products, their docs were never audited.

**Final checks**
- All 7 instantiation gates pass on every difficulty, and traceability is OK on all 5 after publication.
- check_docs prints DOCS OK on all 7 products.
- validate_scenario prints VALID with 0 warnings.
- Merge acceptance found no duplicate personas, identifiers or seed IDs across difficulties.

**Known issues accepted and logged in `worklog.md`**
- Two KB source notes (plan and order) are left open as known blueprint issues. Each is frozen blueprint parameter wording that a difficulty's own rules have since narrowed. Both auditors confirmed the answers are still unique, and no scored value depends on them.
- Market has one latent issue: when a claim reserves a large amount, two guarantee grants on the same order can come out differently depending on which is booked first. Neither task world reaches it, and the auditor marked it not RED.
- Seeded records that no gold step reads are left in place. This is accepted residue (the replay check rejects such rows if added).

**Rulings and changes that affected results**
- For market I made several coordinator rulings:
  - A Northgate-funded promotional gift card can be earned on a marketplace order.
  - Spent promotional value is recovered in proportion to what is refunded. The whole remaining value is recovered when a refund drops the order below the promotion's qualifying total.
  - A restocking fee on a refund where the item isn't returned was struck as unrealistic.
- My own pre-emptive fix in market round 9 created a new defect. I withdrew it and reverted to the round-8 text.
- After all products were published, the cross-product re-check found seeded plan-history rows in plan task 1 and order task 0 that the published plan rules would not produce. Both were re-seeded with the policy and tool files byte-identical. Plan task 1's scored cancellation refund changed from 74.87 to 54.78; order's scored values did not change.

I added a memory note with the lessons from this run (`erl-own-history-seeds-and-preemptive-route-backfire.md`). The worklog has the full record: every start and end, each round, rulings and known issues.
